    A shape $\al$ is $C'$-sparse if the underlying graph (not multigraph) is.
    We will generally say that a graph/shape is sparse if it is $C'$-sparse for some $C'$.
\end{definition}

\begin{definition}[Forbidden subgraph]
    We call a graph $H$ forbidden if it does not occur as a subgraph of $G$.
\end{definition}

